   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Don't Laugh I Love You (Deaner on bass)** (1 other source): Deaner played bass on this song [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Kiss**: back after 89 archived shows (775 days) [4]\n- **Don't Laugh I Love You (Deaner on bass)**: back after 214 archived shows (1540 days); rare: 9 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2003-10-01.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 32 songs; 165 min [1]\n- **ween2003-10-01.MK4.1644**: source not stated; 32 songs; 165 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Uploader's note says the band thought they had a night off after Portland, but learned around 6am of the Seattle gig [2]\n- The pre-show hour was spent in underwear, wandering the club and trying to find a way onto the roof [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2003-10-01.flac16**: taped by unknown; transferred by Lobster; source: Schoeps mk4 Cardioid (110 degrees/stand mounted)> Bill Reutelheuber R-Mod Supply> Sony SBM-1> Sony M1> CD [1]. Also: Original taper says the recording was updated from the master tape, remastered, and given corrected lineage documentation; The update removes the CD-R generation and disc fades from the earlier version [3]\n- **ween2003-10-01.MK4.1644**: taped by Fireball; transferred by Fireball; source: Schoeps MK4's > Billbox Preamp > Sony M1 > DAT Master (44.1kHz/16 bit) [2]. Also: Fireball master field recording, provided as 44.1kHz/16 bit files; numerous tape dropouts were removed, though a few may remain [2]",
